    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math> be distinct points on the parabola <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi></math> such that a circle with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math> as diameter passes through the vertex <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math> of the parabola. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> lies in the first quadrant and the area of the triangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><mi>O</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math> is <math><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi></math>then which of the following is (are) the coordinates of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>?"
